new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9c31b5c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/deployment.md
@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+## Deploying with Kamal
+
+Fizzy ships with a [Kamal](https://kamal-deploy.org/) config for running your own instance on a single Linux server: one container runs the web server, the background jobs (Solid Queue inside Puma) and SQLite, and kamal-proxy terminates SSL with a Let's Encrypt certificate.
+
+### What you need
+
+- A Linux server you can SSH into as root, or as a user that can run Docker. Kamal installs Docker if it's missing.
+- A hostname whose DNS points at the server, with ports 80 and 443 open.
+- An SMTP server for outgoing mail. People sign in with codes sent by email, so mail has to work.
+- Docker on the machine you deploy from, to build the image.
+
+### Configure
+
+1. Edit `config/deploy.yml`:
+   - Replace `fizzy.example.com` with your hostname under `servers`, `proxy.host` and `BASE_URL`.
+   - Set `MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS`, `SMTP_ADDRESS` and `SMTP_PORT` for your mail server. Optional settings are listed there too (`SMTP_DOMAIN`, `SMTP_AUTHENTICATION`, `SMTP_TLS`, `SMTP_ENABLE_STARTTLS_AUTO`).
+   - Change `builder.arch` to `arm64` if your server runs on ARM.
+2. Provide the secrets listed in `.kamal/secrets`. By default they're read from environment variables:
+
+   ```sh
+   export SECRET_KEY_BASE=$(bin/rails secret)
+   export VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=... VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=...   # see "Web Push Notifications" in docs/development.md
+   export SMTP_USERNAME=... SMTP_PASSWORD=...
+   ```
+
+   You can also change `.kamal/secrets` to read them from a password manager. Never commit raw secrets. Keep `SECRET_KEY_BASE` and the VAPID keys the same between deploys.
+
+### Deploy
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal setup    # first time: prepares the server, starts kamal-proxy, and deploys
+bin/kamal deploy   # every deploy after that
+```
+
+Fizzy is then up at `https://your-hostname`. The entrypoint creates or migrates the databases every time the container starts.
+
+### Your data
+
+The SQLite databases (app, jobs, cache, Action Cable) and uploaded files are stored in `/rails/storage`, which is mounted from the `fizzy_storage` Docker volume on the server. That's why data survives deploys and restarts. Back that volume up regularly, for example from `/var/lib/docker/volumes/fizzy_storage/_data`.
+
+### Useful commands
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal console   # Rails console
+bin/kamal shell     # bash in the app container
+bin/kamal logs      # follow the logs
+bin/kamal dbc       # SQLite console
+```
